  "summary_en": "Japan's AI Strategy 2022 sets national AI policy around Society 5.0, adding a Strategic Objective 0 on crisis resilience (disasters, pandemics, planetary issues). It covers implementation in society, education reform, R&D, data infrastructure, digital government, SME support and ethics. Robots appear only incidentally; governance is promotional rather than regulatory.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Adds Strategic Objective 0: AI for National and Planetary Resilience, with digital twins integrated with robotics and sensors.",
   "Promotes Responsible AI, explainable AI and cybersecurity integration to improve AI reliability.",
   "Education targets: AI/data literacy for all high school graduates and about 250,000 applied-skill graduates per year by 2025.",
   "Builds an AI R&D network around core centers (RIKEN AIP, NICT, AIST AIRC).",
   "Ethics: disseminate Human-centered AI Social Principles and pursue international standardization and cooperation, including the GPAI."
